            <ArticleTitle>Radionuclide bone imaging findings in loose cemented joint prostheses appear to be normal postoperative findings in cementless joint prostheses. Preliminary case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>82-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Two cases exemplify that three point uptake on radionuclide bone scans within the first postsurgical year of press-fit cementless joint prostheses appear to be a normal physiomechanical finding.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
